// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 OR MIT
//
// The world JS/TS commands are componentized against. It exports exactly
// Pane's contract and imports its extension data, operations and installed
// applications (wit/extension.wit, wit/data.wit, wit/operations.wit and
// wit/applications.wit, copied into deps/ by the build), and declares the
// WASI 0.3 imports JS source may use: a JS module can import only what this
// world declares. The host bindings are unchanged.
//
// A command whose package.json sets `"pane": { ... }` options also exports
// the interfaces they name: `rootResults` (wit/root-results.wit),
// `indexedResults` (wit/applications.wit) and `operations`
// (wit/operations.wit). The build writes a world `js-command` including
// this one with those exports (tools/componentize-js/pane_js.py).
package pane:js-guest@0.1.0;

world js-extension {
  include pane:extension/extension-with-data@0.1.0;
  import pane:extension/applications@0.1.0;
  import wasi:clocks/monotonic-clock@0.3.0;
}
